Migrating to ESLint’s **flat config** changes both the configuration file and how settings are applied:

- **File name and activation:** Replace legacy `.eslintrc.*` configuration with a file typically named **`eslint.config.js`** at the project root. Flat config is the default in ESLint 9; ESLint 8 supports opting in. [Migration guide](https://eslint.org/docs/latest/use/configure/migration-guide)

- **Exported format:** Export an **array of configuration objects**, rather than one eslintrc-style object. The documentation uses `defineConfig` from `"eslint/config"`:

  ```js
  import { defineConfig } from "eslint/config";

  export default defineConfig([
    {
      files: ["**/*.js"],
      rules: {
        "no-unused-vars": "warn"
      }
    }
  ]);
  ```

  Configuration entries work much like legacy `overrides` blocks, with `files` patterns determining where settings apply. Rule-setting syntax remains unchanged. [Migration guide](https://eslint.org/docs/latest/use/configure/migration-guide)

- **JavaScript imports replace name-based loading:** Plugins and parsers are imported as modules and supplied as objects. Language settings move under `languageOptions`, including parser options and globals; the legacy `env` property is removed. [Migration guide](https://eslint.org/docs/latest/use/configure/migration-guide)

- **Ignored files need attention:** Do not assume legacy `.eslintignore` behavior carries over. Flat config uses configuration-based file selection and an `ignores` mechanism rather than implicit `.eslintignore` semantics. The captured documentation also describes the default JavaScript file patterns as `**/*.{js,mjs,cjs}` when `files` is omitted. [Migration guide](https://eslint.org/docs/latest/use/configure/migration-guide)

